# Extra defaults layered on top of copter.parm (see Dockerfile --defaults list).
#
# Stream-rate defaults (Hz) for SERIAL0 (droneserver/MavSDK) and SERIAL1
# (test-harness readiness probe). A raw SITL binary - unlike a sim_vehicle.py
# setup - has no MAVProxy attached to request telemetry streams, so without
# these the autopilot never sends GLOBAL_POSITION_INT, SYS_STATUS, etc., and
# MavSDK telemetry subscriptions block forever.
SR0_EXT_STAT 2
SR0_POSITION 4
SR0_EXTRA1 4
SR0_EXTRA2 4
SR0_EXTRA3 2
SR0_RAW_SENS 2
SR0_RC_CHAN 2
# Simulated gimbal mount (servo type). Makes the MAVLink gimbal protocol v2
# (GIMBAL_MANAGER/GIMBAL_DEVICE) available so the gimbal tools are testable.
MNT1_TYPE 1
MNT1_PITCH_MIN -90
MNT1_PITCH_MAX 25
# Simulated peripherals so the corresponding plugins are testable:
# downward SITL rangefinder (telemetry.distance_sensor) and an ADS-B receiver
# with 5 simulated aircraft nearby (transponder). NOTE: gripper/winch are
# deliberately NOT enabled - WINCH_TYPE makes ArduPilot report the winch
# "unhealthy" and blocks arming (breaks every flight test), and neither yields
# a working command in SITL anyway (they need a real servo/PWM backend). Their
# coverage is verified at the code path level (docs/coverage_overrides.csv) and
# documented untestable-in-SITL (docs/firmware_notes.csv).
RNGFND1_TYPE 100
RNGFND1_MIN_CM 10
RNGFND1_MAX_CM 4000
RNGFND1_ORIENT 25
ADSB_TYPE 1
SIM_ADSB_COUNT 5
SR1_EXT_STAT 2
SR1_POSITION 4
SR1_EXTRA1 4
SR1_EXTRA2 4
SR1_EXTRA3 2
SR1_RAW_SENS 2
SR1_RC_CHAN 2
